    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d389-a4">

                <pb facs="0697" n="627" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg627"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Viosca to the
                            chief politic and military
                    commander.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Consulate</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1883-02-02"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 2,
                    1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: It has come to the notice of this consulate
                    that Mr. Kirchner, mate of the American schooner Adriana, and three of the crew,
                    have been confined to jail by orders from the district judge.</p>
                <p>I beg of you respectfully to allow a certified copy of the judge’s writ to be
                    issued and forwarded to this consulate.</p>
                <p>With the highest consideration of esteem and respect,</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JAS. VIOSCA,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
